compile-time, template-based tools used to query or modify the properties of types

1. Type Predicates (Querying Value Properties)
Unary Predicates (checks one type): std::is_integral<T>, std::is_pointer<T>, std::is_const<T>.
Binary Predicates (compares two types): std::is_same<T, U>, std::is_convertible<T, U>

2. Property Queries 
std::rank<T>: Returns the number of dimensions of an array type.
std::extent<T>: Returns the size of a specific dimension of an array type.

3. Type Transformations (Modifying Types)
std::remove_const<T> → std::remove_const_t<T>
std::add_pointer<T> → std::add_pointer_t<T>
std::decay<T> → std::decay_t<T>  removes both references and top-level const/volatile qualifiers from a type, while also converting arrays and functions into pointers
